      "aiReviewedAt": "2026-10-15T21:10:02.865602+00:00",
      "aiReviewer": "/root/chemie426_five_existing_visuals_independent",
      "aiNotes": "{\"originalFIRST\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-q2-three-current426-targeted-informed-PAV-review-20261015-v1/FIRSTV2.two-existing-corrected-PNGs-current-context-findings.json\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:cf2e60401298cbaf10890c27a23d3793c3ed2a35b2977314a8b1e8616bda5fc3\",\"bytes\":13808},\"originalOwnRecord\":{\"goalId\":\"ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705\",\"wholeSelectedGoalWithLink\":{\"id\":\"ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705\",\"shortKey\":\"canonical_chemistry_by_amino_acid_nomenclature\",\"title\":\"2-Aminocarbonsäuren systematisch benennen\",\"titleEn\":\"Name 2-amino carboxylic acids systematically\",\"description\":\"Die lernende Person kann einfache 2-Aminocarbonsäuren nach systematischen Nomenklaturregeln benennen.\",\"descriptionEn\":\"The learner can name simple 2-amino carboxylic acids using systematic nomenclature rules.\",\"weight\":1,\"tags\":[\"GK\",\"LK\",\"canonical\",\"SekII\"],\"contains\":[],\"requires\":[\"e9d34f34-2a43-5cc7-bcca-1d08e057531d\"],\"dimensionTags\":{\"framework\":\"canonical-gymnasium-chemistry\",\"demandLevel\":\"AB2\",\"processCompetencies\":[],\"guidingIdeas\":[\"BC_AUFBAU\"],\"phase\":\"Q2\",\"area\":\"Naturstoffe\",\"topicCode\":\"CANONICAL.CHEMISTRY.Q2.AMINO_ACID_NOMENCLATURE\"},\"applicability\":{\"jurisdiction\":[\"DE-BB\",\"DE-BE\",\"DE-BY\",\"DE-HE\",\"DE-MV\",\"DE-NI\",\"DE-TH\"]},\"extendedData\":{\"provenance\":{\"sourceLandscapeId\":\"ff1ca997-b6cc-5ece-8e13-5498b4bbf808\",\"sourceLandscapeTitle\":\"DE-BY - Chemie Gymnasium (Bayern, LehrplanPLUS Source-Extraction)\",\"sourceGoalId\":\"4ccb88b1-c6cf-5931-af49-7c03f43ce2f3\"}},\"type\":\"atomic\",\"examples\":[],\"resourceLinks\":[{\"type\":\"goal-visualization\",\"resourceType\":\"image\",\"role\":\"primary\",\"skillpilotId\":\"ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705\",\"title\":\"Visualisierung: 2-Aminocarbonsäuren systematisch benennen\",\"url\":\"/assets/goal-visualizations/chemie/ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705/ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705.png\",\"provider\":\"OpenAI / ChatGPT-Codex built-in image_gen (model version not exposed)\",\"description\":\"Visualisierung zum Lernziel: 2-Aminocarbonsäuren systematisch benennen.\",\"altText\":\"Die vereinfachten Strukturformeln von Glycin und Alanin markieren den Carboxyl-Kohlenstoff als C1 und den benachbarten alpha-Kohlenstoff als C2. Die Aminogruppe sitzt jeweils an C2.\",\"lang\":\"de\",\"license\":\"CC-BY-4.0\",\"reviewStatus\":\"pilot\"}]},\"verdict\":\"KEEP\",\"vResult\":\"PASS_FOR_THIS_EXACT_ORIENTATION_IMAGE_IN_THIS_SELECTED_CONTEXT\",\"nativeFindings\":[\"Glycine is drawn NH2−CH2−COOH, withC2 pointing to the CH2 carbon andC1 to carboxyl carbon. Alanine has CH3−CH(NH2)−COOH, and bothC1/C2 arrows again point to the corresponding carbon letters.\",\"The short label Amino anC2 agrees with both formulas. The NH2 branch belongs to the alpha carbon; there is no extra carbonyl carbon or stereochemical assignment. Trivial names orient the examples without replacing systematic naming.\"],\"nativeViewedWithViewImage\":true,\"actualScreensViewedWithViewImage\":[{\"containerWidth\":360,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-q2-three-current426-targeted-informed-PAV-review-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705.container-360.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:89743edaf23fecb2da573ff5c27e78f0ee6af7bd562898e3cada1723f0372fa4\",\"bytes\":93139},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1672,\"naturalHeight\":941,\"imageElementWidth\":316,\"imageElementHeight\":177.84375,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":315.99867162592983,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":177.84375,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705\"}},{\"containerWidth\":680,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-q2-three-current426-targeted-informed-PAV-review-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705.container-680.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:aca9c98fc5e7c1ba06a292bc030009e52b80d07c0cfe0ac514e111efd7374fa7\",\"bytes\":257468},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1672,\"naturalHeight\":941,\"imageElementWidth\":636,\"imageElementHeight\":357.9375,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":635.9952178533474,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":357.9375,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/ffec1761-c954-5b5d-a0cf-4c8367f91705\"}}],\"formatDecision\":\"Keep the existing1672×941 landscapePNG. At316×177.84 and636×357.94px the formulas, relevant charges/arrows and labels remain visible, with no cropped molecule or label. The448px height bound is not reached. No provider or ratio replacement is justified.\",\"altConsistency\":\"The whole selected ALT accurately describes the shown formulas and the intended comparison; no quantitative measurement or stereochemistry claim is added.\",\"contextBoundary\":\"Image correctness does not approve all P material, actual learner performance, source coverage, D text or M status. In particular the b47 P case-2 HOLD remains open independently of this KEEP.\",\"blockingImageDefects\":[],\"normalQaWrites\":0,\"imageChanges\":0,\"HumanApproval\":false,\"HumanTrial\":false},\"technicalBoundary\":\"Original independent V only; no new science or human approval.\"}"
