      "aiReviewedAt": "2026-10-15T21:10:02.865602+00:00",
      "aiReviewer": "/root/chemie426_five_existing_visuals_independent",
      "aiNotes": "{\"originalFIRST\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-q2-three-current426-targeted-informed-PAV-review-20261015-v1/FIRSTV2.two-existing-corrected-PNGs-current-context-findings.json\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:cf2e60401298cbaf10890c27a23d3793c3ed2a35b2977314a8b1e8616bda5fc3\",\"bytes\":13808},\"originalOwnRecord\":{\"goalId\":\"b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab\",\"wholeSelectedGoalWithLink\":{\"id\":\"b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab\",\"shortKey\":\"canonical_chemistry_by_amino_acid_side_chain_classification\",\"title\":\"Aminocarbonsäuren nach Restfunktionalität klassifizieren\",\"titleEn\":\"Classify amino carboxylic acids by side-chain functionality\",\"description\":\"Die lernende Person kann Aminocarbonsäuren anhand der Funktionalität ihrer Seitenketten gruppieren und beobachtbare Eigenschaften aus den unterschiedlichen Resten erklären.\",\"descriptionEn\":\"The learner can group amino carboxylic acids by side-chain functionality and explain observable properties from different residues.\",\"weight\":1,\"tags\":[\"GK\",\"LK\",\"canonical\",\"SekII\"],\"contains\":[],\"requires\":[\"e9d34f34-2a43-5cc7-bcca-1d08e057531d\"],\"dimensionTags\":{\"framework\":\"canonical-gymnasium-chemistry\",\"demandLevel\":\"AB2\",\"processCompetencies\":[],\"guidingIdeas\":[\"BC_AUFBAU\"],\"phase\":\"Q2\",\"area\":\"Naturstoffe\",\"topicCode\":\"CANONICAL.CHEMISTRY.Q2.AMINO_ACID_SIDE_CHAIN_CLASSIFICATION\"},\"applicability\":{\"jurisdiction\":[\"DE-BB\",\"DE-BE\",\"DE-BY\",\"DE-HB\",\"DE-HE\",\"DE-MV\",\"DE-NI\",\"DE-RP\",\"DE-SH\",\"DE-SL\",\"DE-SN\",\"DE-ST\",\"DE-TH\"]},\"extendedData\":{\"provenance\":{\"sourceLandscapeId\":\"ff1ca997-b6cc-5ece-8e13-5498b4bbf808\",\"sourceLandscapeTitle\":\"DE-BY - Chemie Gymnasium (Bayern, LehrplanPLUS Source-Extraction)\",\"sourceGoalId\":\"474db408-a366-52bd-b1d2-47772ce8b677\"}},\"type\":\"atomic\",\"examples\":[],\"resourceLinks\":[{\"type\":\"goal-visualization\",\"resourceType\":\"image\",\"role\":\"primary\",\"skillpilotId\":\"b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab\",\"title\":\"Visualisierung: Aminocarbonsäuren nach Restfunktionalität klassifizieren\",\"url\":\"/assets/goal-visualizations/chemie/b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab/b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab.png\",\"provider\":\"OpenAI / ChatGPT-Codex built-in image_gen (model version not exposed)\",\"description\":\"Visualisierung zum Lernziel: Aminocarbonsäuren nach Restfunktionalität klassifizieren.\",\"altText\":\"Alanin und Serin sind bei pH7 als Zwitterionmodelle mit gemeinsamen NH3+- und COO−-Gruppen dargestellt. Ihre Seitenketten CH3 und CH2OH unterscheiden sich; Wassertropfen umgeben beide Moleküle.\",\"lang\":\"de\",\"license\":\"CC-BY-4.0\",\"reviewStatus\":\"pilot\"}]},\"verdict\":\"KEEP\",\"vResult\":\"PASS_FOR_THIS_EXACT_ORIENTATION_IMAGE_IN_THIS_SELECTED_CONTEXT\",\"nativeFindings\":[\"At the explicitly statedpH7, both alanine and serine show shared NH3+ and COO− groups. Their alpha carbon has four connected groups; side chains are correctly CH3 versusCH2OH. Water droplets surround both amino acids, with additional access to serine OH; there is no claim that alanine is wholly water-insoluble.\",\"No exact hydration-shell orientation, whole-molecule solubility ranking or D/L assignment is drawn. The image supports residue functionality while preserving common ionizable groups.\"],\"nativeViewedWithViewImage\":true,\"actualScreensViewedWithViewImage\":[{\"containerWidth\":360,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-q2-three-current426-targeted-informed-PAV-review-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab.container-360.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:a8c979428236617f15ca6f3c9916773604fd38874504f92f09b951de8ca98e19\",\"bytes\":92959},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1672,\"naturalHeight\":941,\"imageElementWidth\":316,\"imageElementHeight\":177.84375,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":315.99867162592983,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":177.84375,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab\"}},{\"containerWidth\":680,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-q2-three-current426-targeted-informed-PAV-review-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab.container-680.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:ce1bb676a4edf7ed4aa0a93aa90cefbfb4cc51a084eeb33f296db5b0486ff8f3\",\"bytes\":257628},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1672,\"naturalHeight\":941,\"imageElementWidth\":636,\"imageElementHeight\":357.9375,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":635.9952178533474,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":357.9375,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/b47d542d-c2d7-5554-95dc-10b47ab622ab\"}}],\"formatDecision\":\"Keep the existing1672×941 landscapePNG. At316×177.84 and636×357.94px the formulas, relevant charges/arrows and labels remain visible, with no cropped molecule or label. The448px height bound is not reached. No provider or ratio replacement is justified.\",\"altConsistency\":\"The whole selected ALT accurately describes the shown formulas and the intended comparison; no quantitative measurement or stereochemistry claim is added.\",\"contextBoundary\":\"Image correctness does not approve all P material, actual learner performance, source coverage, D text or M status. In particular the b47 P case-2 HOLD remains open independently of this KEEP.\",\"blockingImageDefects\":[],\"normalQaWrites\":0,\"imageChanges\":0,\"HumanApproval\":false,\"HumanTrial\":false},\"technicalBoundary\":\"Original independent V only; no new science or human approval.\"}"
