      "aiReviewer": "Independent Codex actual-PNG reviewer / chemie_methods4_fresh_science_20261016",
      "aiNotes": "Independent actual PNG KEEP; native1672x941 and whole360x203/680x383 were actually viewed. The TLC startline is above the solvent surface; the plate bottom contacts the mobile phase. The dashed solvent front stops below the plate top. The upward mobile-phase arrow and stationary-phase pointer distinguish the two phases. The two inset measurement arrows a and b share the same startline. The purple a ends at the purple spot-height guide; b ends at the solvent-front guide. Both are distances along the same migration direction and a<b, consistent with dimensionless Rf=a/b. The measurement inset is slightly proportionally rescaled rather than aligned pixel-for-pixel with the plate. Approximate visual coordinates: main baseline609/front178/purplecentre356 gives253/431≈0.587; inset baseline609/front197/purpleguide367 gives242/412≈0.587. Drawing/spot-blur tolerance applies; these are illustration checks, not lab measurements. Thus both endpoints represent the same relative migration. A, B and U visibly share one baseline; upper/lower U spots match the illustrated reference heights under the same pictured conditions. Neither co-migration nor two visible spots is labeled as proof of unique identity, purity, exactly two components or universal Rf. The large Rf fraction and proportional arrows carry the mathematical relation without units. Colored b and the green lower spots do not contradict its endpoint: b visibly terminates at the front guide, not at that spot. Frozen scientific authority: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-16/chemie-source2-electrophoresis-and-planar-theory-two-PNG-independent-V-20261016-v1/SCIENCE-FIRST.actual-two-PNG-independent-visual-and-bounded-P-compatibility.json sha256:c8ca4c14ff643ee993dcf4dee479d57f380544a0ad90761f808a0dc62d5f7f40. Image compatibility only; no full P/source/D/A/M/kind approval, learner execution, human approval or M7 completion."
