      "aiReviewer": "Independent Codex actual-PNG reviewer / chemie_methods4_fresh_science_20261016",
      "aiNotes": "Independent actual PNG KEEP; native1672x941 and whole360x203/680x383 were actually viewed. The power source and chamber consistently label left negative/black and right positive/red. Both wires preserve that assignment. Both illustrated dye spots carry minus signs and the indicated migration points from the start toward the positive/right electrode: correct for the selected negative dye model. It is not a claim that every amino acid is negative or that anions always travel to the physical right; reversing the poles reverses that side. The separate planning card shows pH and plus/minus signs without direction arrows. It leaves charge-state/pH/polarity reasoning open rather than drawing incompatible universal migration directions. The chamber is depicted schematically covered with transparent frame/reflections, connectors outside the cover and no handling person. This is a closed-model illustration, not a certification that a real apparatus or local safety protocol is approved. The Rohdaten notebook is visibly empty and accompanied by a question symbol. No measured pH, voltage, time or distance, actual observation, learner conduct or successful separation is asserted. The gel spots are illustrative, never learner raw data. No actor is present; there is no erroneous person-facing notebook/board/scale orientation. Decorative books and the background note impose no extra assessed content. Frozen scientific authority: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-16/chemie-source2-electrophoresis-and-planar-theory-two-PNG-independent-V-20261016-v1/SCIENCE-FIRST.actual-two-PNG-independent-visual-and-bounded-P-compatibility.json sha256:c8ca4c14ff643ee993dcf4dee479d57f380544a0ad90761f808a0dc62d5f7f40. Image compatibility only; no full P/source/D/A/M/kind approval, learner execution, human approval or M7 completion. Actual practical373 P remains separate/pending; an empty notebook is no execution proof."
