      "aiNotes": "Actual current asset/text-fit science: The existing JPG shows the conjugate base/acid ratio with an acetate example, 0.20/0.10 and pKa4.76 giving pH5.06. This supports the newly explicit ratio method. It is a teaching example, not a claim that all buffers obey the concentration formula exactly; the unchanged independent cases/profile assess the approximation limits. Absence of a full limits checklist in the image is not itself a defect. Full independent A6 and B judgments bound at curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-14/chemie-acid7-current419-paired-D6-retained059-P7A7M2V1-inactive-integration-technical-20261014-v4/V/V3.actual-source-judgments-and-QA-fielddiffs.json. Original/human history unchanged. PNG481 is a newly reviewed asset, not a retagged old approval; existing two JPGs retained after genuine text-fit review."
