      "aiReviewer": "Codex independent chemistry reviewer /root/chemie426_five_existing_visuals_independent",
      "aiNotes": "{\"sourceFIRST\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-caption-successor-informed-independent-V1-20261015-v1/FIRSTV1.actual-caption-corrected-PNG-current-whole-context.json\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:233100b706598074294487ed34fb44035cc04acc03e25176d4dcfb2441cd8a03\",\"bytes\":12744},\"originalWholeIndependentVRecord\":{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"role\":\"Genuine first own informed independent V1 on actual corrected caption raster and current whole goal context\",\"reviewer\":\"Codex independent chemistry reviewer /root/chemie426_five_existing_visuals_independent\",\"reviewedAtUTC\":\"2026-10-15T21:43:13.422093+00:00\",\"goalId\":\"96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\",\"wholeGoal\":{\"id\":\"96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\",\"shortKey\":\"canonical_chemistry_upper_carbohydrate_reducing_glucose_assays\",\"title\":\"Reduzierende Kohlenhydrate und Glucose nachweisen\",\"titleEn\":\"Detect reducing carbohydrates and glucose\",\"description\":\"Die lernende Person kann ausgewählte Nachweise für reduzierende Kohlenhydrate und für Glucose durchführen, auswerten und ihre unterschiedliche Aussagekraft anhand von Molekülstruktur und Enzymwirkung erklären.\",\"descriptionEn\":\"The learner can perform and evaluate selected assays for reducing carbohydrates and for glucose, and explain their differing analytical scope using molecular structure and enzyme action.\",\"phase\":\"Q2\",\"area\":\"Naturstoffe\",\"level\":2,\"core\":true,\"weight\":1,\"tags\":[\"GK\",\"LK\",\"SekII\",\"canonical\"],\"requires\":[\"1d2e7b80-653d-57b8-a284-8ede5a353b73\",\"363c5740-8a3c-50b8-8c3a-5548c80c36ea\"],\"contains\":[],\"examples\":[],\"applicability\":{\"jurisdiction\":[\"DE-BW\",\"DE-BY\",\"DE-HB\",\"DE-HE\",\"DE-NI\",\"DE-RP\",\"DE-SH\",\"DE-SL\",\"DE-SN\",\"DE-TH\"]},\"type\":\"atomic\",\"topicCode\":\"CANONICAL.CHEMISTRY.Q2.CARBOHYDRATE_REDUCING_GLUCOSE_ASSAYS\",\"dimensionTags\":{\"framework\":\"canonical-gymnasium-chemistry\",\"demandLevel\":\"AB2\",\"processCompetencies\":[\"PK1_EXPERIMENTIEREN\",\"PK2_MODELLIEREN\"],\"guidingIdeas\":[\"BC_AUFBAU\",\"BC_REAKTION\"],\"phase\":\"Q2\",\"area\":\"Naturstoffe\",\"topicCode\":\"CANONICAL.CHEMISTRY.Q2.CARBOHYDRATE_REDUCING_GLUCOSE_ASSAYS\"},\"extendedData\":{\"provenance\":{\"sourceLandscapeTitle\":\"Chemie Kursstufe (Baden-Wuerttemberg, BP2016 V2 Source-Extraction)\",\"sourceGoalId\":\"bw-chem-sekii-3-4-4-b05-a01-ea028f8b\",\"sourceGoalTitle\":\"BW 3.4.4 (5): D-Glucose, Maltose und Saccharose auf ihre reduzierende Wirkung untersuchen (Benedict-Probe oder...\",\"sourceRef\":\"Bildungsplan 2016 Gymnasium Chemie Baden-Wuerttemberg, 3.4.4 (5), S. 34.\",\"sourceSpan\":\"3.4.4 (5)\"}},\"resourceLinks\":[{\"type\":\"goal-visualization\",\"resourceType\":\"image\",\"role\":\"primary\",\"skillpilotId\":\"96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\",\"title\":\"Visualisierung: Reduzierende Kohlenhydrate und Glucose nachweisen\",\"url\":\"/assets/goal-visualizations/chemie/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a.png\",\"provider\":\"OpenAI / ChatGPT-Codex built-in image generation; precise edit of existing SkillPilot illustration\",\"description\":\"Vorhandene Zweiteilung aus nicht glucosespezifischem Kupfer-Nachweis und enzymatischem Glucose-Nachweis; die negative Beschriftung besagt nun nicht nachgewiesen statt absolute Abwesenheit.\",\"altText\":\"Links zeigt die Kupferprobe ein positives ziegelrotes Cu(I)-oxid-Ergebnis und ein blau bleibendes negatives Ergebnis mit der begrenzten Beschriftung „Negativ: nicht nachgewiesen“. Sie ist nicht glucosespezifisch. Rechts steht der schematische GOD/POD-Signalweg für einen enzymatischen Glucosenachweis; die Reagenz-/Signalfolge ist keine bilanzierte stöchiometrische Gleichung. Keine echte Messung oder absolute Abwesenheitsbehauptung.\",\"lang\":\"de\",\"license\":\"CC-BY-4.0\",\"reviewStatus\":\"candidate\"}]},\"verdict\":\"KEEP\",\"authorSelector\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-claim-one-caption-image-author-successor-20261015-v1/NEUTRAL.finite96-one-negative-caption-image-author.selector.json\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:0a7ff709fd9241c98f44ba49119bf823bc5409275dadcc09e93a7be521f582c1\",\"bytes\":2064},\"actualPNG\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-claim-one-caption-image-author-successor-20261015-v1/images/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:fae7aa63c39e3debf1e06870a69b6283e013d6d0a96d96068a768d99fee3d351\",\"bytes\":1676750},\"nativeSighting\":{\"method\":\"view_image with detail=original, actual author PNG directly viewed\",\"width\":1678,\"height\":937,\"actuallyViewed\":true},\"actualGoalCardScreens\":[{\"language\":\"de\",\"containerWidth\":360,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-caption-successor-informed-independent-V1-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a.de.container-360.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:0337d01feb54165acbbe8eaa11dc1ba3f6ff0ab91063f9433926ad821b6e79e0\",\"bytes\":94830},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1678,\"naturalHeight\":937,\"imageElementWidth\":316,\"imageElementHeight\":176.453125,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":315.9960979188901,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":176.453125,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\"},\"actuallyViewedWithViewImage\":true},{\"language\":\"de\",\"containerWidth\":680,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-caption-successor-informed-independent-V1-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a.de.container-680.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:6d1427ac446a071694a4b2f2cfb317a2289683e4380c6c91b50fe0649a8f7b10\",\"bytes\":274450},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1678,\"naturalHeight\":937,\"imageElementWidth\":636,\"imageElementHeight\":355.140625,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":635.9935632337247,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":355.140625,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\"},\"actuallyViewedWithViewImage\":true},{\"language\":\"en\",\"containerWidth\":360,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-caption-successor-informed-independent-V1-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a.en.container-360.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:6329c9d88657381678ab9f27ff7a85f4829a3b9670d6da6a6dcaaf442b09d4cc\",\"bytes\":89995},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1678,\"naturalHeight\":937,\"imageElementWidth\":316,\"imageElementHeight\":176.453125,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":315.9960979188901,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":176.453125,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\"},\"actuallyViewedWithViewImage\":true},{\"language\":\"en\",\"containerWidth\":680,\"screenshot\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-caption-successor-informed-independent-V1-20261015-v1/browser/GoalCard.96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a.en.container-680.png\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:6ffd2fd0a219176a54f5ffcf9b88f8dc1382a6842535624569a6b6ccc1257422\",\"bytes\":270391},\"metrics\":{\"naturalWidth\":1678,\"naturalHeight\":937,\"imageElementWidth\":636,\"imageElementHeight\":355.140625,\"objectFit\":\"contain\",\"maxHeight\":\"448px\",\"actualContainedRasterWidth\":635.9935632337247,\"actualContainedRasterHeight\":355.140625,\"complete\":true,\"currentSrc\":\"http://127.0.0.1:5173/review-assets/96d33fb6-ed14-50ab-b5c7-5ce0559d518a\"},\"actuallyViewedWithViewImage\":true}],\"actualCaptureReceipt\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie96-negative-caption-successor-informed-independent-V1-20261015-v1/browser/RECEIPT.actual-unchanged-GoalCard-360-680.json\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:b3abcc2adb5ad5c920133666bd3f569f113673e395672ea117c6f82105c86687\",\"bytes\":7921},\"concreteFindings\":[\"The actual negative caption now reads Bleibt blau (Negativ: nicht nachgewiesen). The blue outcome is described as non-detection rather than proof that reducing sugar is absent; the original specific REVISE defect is resolved in these new pixels.\",\"The two-panel copper-test versus GOD/POD comparison remains visually intact. The left retains blue Cu(II) sample/reagent, warming, red Cu(I)-oxide precipitate, an unchanged blue negative vessel, and the not-glucose-specific label. The right retains glucose/oxygen to gluconolactone/peroxide and the POD-coupled color-signal sequence.\",\"The right POD notation remains an unbalanced schematic reagent/signal sequence, with Farbiges Signal rather than a chemical product species. No enzyme count, balanced reaction, disappearance graphic or explicit consumption claim is shown. It does not create a new enzyme-consumption REVISE. It must not be taught as a balanced stoichiometric equation.\",\"The corrected caption and the distinct analytical scope are compatible with the current complete DE/EN goal and the already reviewed three-case profile. The visual is an orientation diagram, not an assay protocol, full selectivity/interference guarantee or actual learner result.\",\"Native1678x937 is sufficient to read the corrected wording and inspect both pathways. The current GoalCard contains the full image at316x176.453 and636x355.141px with no crop and a448px maximum-height rule that is not reached. At316px the detailed labels remain small; the two assay branches and signal contrast are visible. At636px the caption is readily inspectable. Text density is a documented format limit, not a reason to replace the preserved useful image.\",\"The new PNG is a rerasterized author edit, not a byte-identical copy of the old JPEG. The wide ratio and composition are preserved visually; no unchanged surrounding-pixel-byte assertion is made.\"],\"wholeGoalContextDelta\":\"All whole-goal fields except resourceLinks are independently equal to the previously reviewed two-text96 successor. New URL, ALT, provider and image description bind this actual PNG and accurately describe non-detection and the schematic POD sequence.\",\"formatDecision\":{\"decision\":\"KEEP_EXISTING_AUTHOR_PNG_AND_WIDE_COMPOSITION\",\"width\":1678,\"height\":937,\"imageEditedOrGeneratedByReviewer\":false,\"newRatioOrRedesignNeeded\":false},\"languageAndMethodBoundary\":\"Both exact authored DE and EN title/description props were rendered through the actual unchanged GoalCard at360/680px. Existing German image labels remain. The EN prop selection is explicitly a component-context capture, not a Native loader/D/translation-pipeline approval.\",\"priorScientificBoundaries\":{\"PAndAContextSciencePreserved\":true,\"priorSelector\":{\"path\":\"curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-15/chemie-two-local-text-successors-informed-PAV-context-20261015-v1/OUTPUTS.finite-two-local-texts-informed-PAV-context.selector.json\",\"sha256\":\"sha256:3054d17cc3eaca9e44db51ca5d74d6654363afb832c5929d38d53e62608a93d8\",\"bytes\":4912},\"newPReviews\":0,\"newAReviews\":0,\"newDReviews\":0,\"newMReviews\":0,\"actualPerformEvidenceAdded\":false,\"sourceCoverageExpanded\":false,\"memoryChanged\":false},\"historicalTruth\":\"The original JPEG remains unchanged and its earlier REVISE remains a valid sealed judgment on that original negative-caption claim. This positive judgment applies only to the exact new PNG in the bound current goal context.\",\"normalVRecordsWritten\":0,\"actualLaboratoryMeasurement\":false,\"observedLearnerWork\":null,\"HumanApproval\":false,\"HumanTrial\":false,\"trialStatus\":\"noHumanTrial\"},\"technicalBoundary\":\"Genuine aktuelle Kontextsicht, keine Humanfreigabe/keine neue P/A/M/D-Wissenschaft.\"}"
